## Priority When Rules Overlap

1. **`wetar-audio-and-storage.mdc`** wins for user file safety, strict folder-whitelist isolation, scanning, Drift schema, and cache boundaries.
2. **`wetar-personalization-and-theming.mdc`** and **`wetar-mandatory-design.mdc`** win for tokens, dynamic colors, typography, player backgrounds, and RTL/LTR rules.
3. **`wetar-engineering-quality.mdc`** wins for audio stability, isolate offloading, screen-off idle CPU, performance/RAM/size budgets, and zero-warning analysis.
4. **`english-comments-only.mdc`** wins for developer text language (English) and user copy (`AppLocalizations` only).
5. **`wetar-bloc-and-structure.mdc`**, **`wetar-interaction-ux.mdc`**, **`wetar-platforms-flutter.mdc`**, and **`git-commits.mdc`** govern architecture, UX behavior, OS integration, and git commits.

